{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216454-how-to-cast-magick-divided-successes-and-otherwise","id":1216454,"title":"How to cast magick, divided successes and otherwise?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-07T20:19:41-07:00","id":1216454,"title":"How to cast magick, divided successes and otherwise?","content":"Hey, so going through the book, I've encountered a serious issue. The book is very frustratingly unclear on just how the hell one determines the successes required for an effect, at least to me. I think a few examples might help, and could allow the more experienced people here to correct my misunderstandings.<br /> <br /> Let's keep it simple. Last session I was in, two players wanted to turn invisible, by having one of them cast a forces effect. To do this and still be able to see would ordinarily be Correspondence 1, forces 2 if affecting only the caster, and becomes correspondence 2 forces 3 to affect another target? And what is the base successes? Is it a standard feat? Difficult? It requires 2 successes minimum to affect someone besides the caster. Let's say 2 so I can continue this example. So we have a Vulgar Forces 3 effect that requires 2 successes due to that being the minimum required to make the effect work, and there's no additional successes required to affect the caster +1 or to have it work for a scene as the two successes required will apply evenly to targets, durarion, and base effect? Or does it require 2 base, +1 for duration, and +1 for targets, making it 4?<br /> <br /> Okay, long-winded first example of my confusion, sorry. Another thing: the book has this set of lines in the &quot;quick reference&quot;, spread out to look like seperate paragraphs: &quot;Additional Damage, Targets, or Duration may be purchased under the Optional Dividing Successes Rule, below. <br /> <br /> &quot;If you wish to add to the Effect\u2019s Damage, Targets, or Duration before you make the roll, figure out how many additional successes you would need, declare them to the Storyteller, and then roll the total amount (that is, the Base + additional successes).&quot;<br /> <br /> Is the part about additional successes the &quot;divided successes&quot; option, or a base rule for having a spell do more or last longer than just what the base successes would give you by baking in the power initially? My confusion stems from the fact that the &quot;divided successes&quot; rule is a paragraph of text below that, and so I am unsure what the line in the QR chart means by &quot;below&quot; <br /> <br /> How do correspondence ranges affect the successes required? Do they also get successes applied evenly? Would that same invisibility effect, cast using correspondence on a target that is very familiar or that they have a close connection to require still just two successes, or do the correspondence successes get added on top? Does this mean the base damage or duration of such an effect is 4 successes worth? Would a lightning bolt cast in the same way deal 8 health levels by default? <br /> <br /> I suppose the major difficulty is in understanding how and why successes apply and where. If one makes a complex and reflexive multiple sensation mental illusion, does it automatically last 6 months unless the player wants it to last for less? Etc. Etc. I don't understand, and the more I read, the less clear it gets. Please help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","user":"PixelPuzzler","date":". 05-07-2018, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T22:44:42-07:00","id":1216500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixelPuzzler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1216454-how-to-cast-magick-divided-successes-and-otherwise#post1216454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, so going through the book, I've encountered a serious issue. The book is very frustratingly unclear on just how the hell one determines the successes required for an effect, at least to me. I think a few examples might help, and could allow the more experienced people here to correct my misunderstandings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Myes. The amount of base successes required is rather up to the ST in question. There is a rough table on page 302.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's keep it simple. Last session I was in, two players wanted to turn invisible, by having one of them cast a forces effect. To do this and still be able to see would ordinarily be Correspondence 1, forces 2 if affecting only the caster, and becomes correspondence 2 forces 3 to affect another target? And what is the base successes? Is it a standard feat? Difficult? It requires 2 successes minimum to affect someone besides the caster. Let's say 2 so I can continue this example. So we have a Vulgar Forces 3 effect that requires 2 successes due to that being the minimum required to make the effect work, and there's no additional successes required to affect the caster +1 or to have it work for a scene as the two successes required will apply evenly to targets, durarion, and base effect? Or does it require 2 base, +1 for duration, and +1 for targets, making it 4? </div> </div> </div>Ah, no, let's take this step by step:<br /> <br /> * Forces 2 stays forces 2. You are bending light in either case, even if used on others, so this does not change.<br /> <br /> * Correspondence 2 in either case, as you basically are trying to sense things that are out of sight or blocked by a nearby obstacle (in this case the obstacle being the bent away light). You are also potentially going to use that Forces 2 effect on the other person while they are out of sight - and Correspondence needs to be at the level of the highest other sphere used remotely, so Forces 2 = Correspondence 2.<br /> <br /> * To make the invisibility cloak stay around yourself, no Life sphere is required. However if you want to make it automatically move with the other person in a way you don't need to concentrate on it nonstop requires locking the effect on the other - this requires the Life sphere. According to &quot;How Do You Do That&quot;, this actually requires Life 4 to lock onto another person. Without the locking, your character must be able to keep a metaphysical eye on the other person, and concentrate on moving it with them. This makes the running spell counts against the limit of two running spells-that-demand-concentration limit before casting the next effect becomes harder to cast, getting a +1 difficlty increase. (See page 528/529, 'How Many Effects can I use at once)<br /> <br /> * The amount of succesess required is, according to the table on page 302 roughly a 3, I'd say. This would also give it enough duration to last for a while, unless you are using the Divided Successes chart..then you need 3 base successes, PLUS whatever you put into duration, PLUS one for the additional target. The Divded Successes rule was the default in Revised, and it caused requiring extended rolls and rituals for the most simplest of things at times - which is why I would only use it in case you need both, damage AND duration, in one effect, as this can only be done with that rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is the part about additional successes the &quot;divided successes&quot; option </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's about the Divided Successes rule.<br /> By default, the *total* amount of sucessses you have counts for everything in one: damage or-duration, range and amount of targets (minus one since affecting another already requires 2 successes), and needs to be a certain minimum according to the table on page 302.<br /> As I wrote above, I'd only use the Divided Successes rule for effects that require both, damage AND duration, since it's the only way to get that handled.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do correspondence ranges affect the successes required? </div> </div> </div>The correspondence targets determine the minimum amount of successes required. If a spell would normally require 2 base successes, but the correspondence range table requires a higher amount, it moves up to that amount. Again, unless you use the Divided Success rule, where it becomes Base Successes + Successes spent on range instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do they also get successes applied evenly? Would that same invisibility effect, cast using correspondence on a target that is very familiar or that they have a close connection to require still just two successes, or do the correspondence successes get added on top? Does this mean the base damage or duration of such an effect is 4 successes worth? Would a lightning bolt cast in the same way deal 8 health levels by default? </div> </div> </div>See above <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> To leave it simple:<br /> * Without Divided Successes: Total success count for every aspect of the effect. The only exception is wanting Damage AND Duration in one effect, which requires adding one or the other as extra successes on the top.<br /> * With Divded Successes: Everything needs adding up. Base Successes needed + Damage + Range + Duration + Targets. Which, again, makes even small effects at times require extended rolls or rituals, hence the suggestion to only use this for adding duration to a damage effect, or damage to an effect with duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-08-2018, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}